    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The Casa Grande deposit (also known as the Santa Cruz deposit) is a buried porphyry copper deposit 7 mi west of the city of Casa Grande, Arizona. The prospect has been drilled at close spacing and ore was discovered between 1,000 and 2,000 ft below the surface. The deposit is similar to the Sacaton porphyry copper deposit located 6 mi northeast and may have been part of the same hydrotherraal system that was later separated by faulting.\"",
